# Generated outputs (recreated by `make train` / `make benchmark`).
#
# Most stay out of git. The exceptions below are committed on purpose: they are
# what the served app reads at runtime, so a plain "Download ZIP" from GitHub
# produces a working demo instead of one that refuses to start. Roughly 11 MB
# raw, ~7.5 MB packed — small enough to be worth the convenience, and this is a
# thesis artefact rather than a repository that retrains on a schedule.
#
# artifacts/ is committed (4 MB): the model, calibrator, thresholds, feature
# list, metadata and the ADR regressor the /predict path uses.
#
# artifacts/ph/ is NOT. It is fitted on the Punta Villa PMS export — real
# reservations that are deliberately absent from this repository — and the
# Portugal demo never loads it. Regenerate it with scripts/training/train_ph.py
# if you hold that CSV.
artifacts/ph/

reports/*
!reports/.gitkeep

# Reports the app reads: hero banner, benchmarks tab, SHAP table, training date.
!reports/metrics.json
!reports/champion_summary.json
!reports/segment_metrics.json
!reports/segment_metrics.csv
!reports/dedup_sensitivity.json
!reports/benchmarks/
!reports/dedup/
!reports/thesis/
!reports/cv/
!reports/ph/

# Evidence for figures in the paper that no other committed file carries: the
# deposit-type and field ablations, and the pipeline's own verdict on each hypothesis.
!reports/deposit_ablation.json
!reports/field_ablation.json
!reports/hypothesis_summary.json

# ...but never the Philippine row-level output. Each row is one real Punta
# Villa reservation, and the per-record SHAP plot draws one point per booking.
# Aggregate JSONs are committed so the PH notebooks render; the rows are not.
# This is the rule docs/provenance.md states.
reports/ph/*predictions*.csv
reports/ph/shap_summary_plot.png

# Figures: only the curated publication set the UI embeds, not all 190.
# The directory has to be re-included before anything inside it can be.
!reports/figures/
reports/figures/*
!reports/figures/.gitkeep
!reports/figures/essential/

data/*.csv
!data/.gitkeep
!data/hotel_bookings.csv
# Live prediction stores (sqlite/CSV written at serving time by the UI and
# FastAPI /predict, read by Power BI — never tracked)
data/predictions/
*.sqlite

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Manuscripts, drafts and presentation material — kept locally, never in the
# code repository. This repo holds the pipeline; the write-up lives elsewhere.
/*.pdf
*.docx
*.pptx
docs/thesis_drafts/
docs/defense/
